          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em apartness relation
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            that, instead of saying when two things are the same (as an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
          %p
            Apartness relations are most used in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
          %p
            The apartness relations that we discuss here are sometimes called
            = succeed "," do
              %strong point–point apartness
            %em set–set
            or
            %em point–set
            apartness relations; see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+space"} proximity space
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+space"} apartness space
            (respectively) for these.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#abstract Abstract
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with an
            %strong apartness relation
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as the set of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi TV
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV^\op
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} poset
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth values
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            using
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            (which says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV
            is self-dual under
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            (which makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            a groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over the cartesian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV
            = succeed ")." do
              %em itself
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            (or interpreted
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internally
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi TV
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV^\op
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+algebra"} co-Heyting algebra
          %h3#concrete Concrete
          %p
            Of course, nobody but a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theorist
            would use the above as a
            %em definition
            of an apartness relation. Normally, one defines an apartness relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
            satisfying these three properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreflexive+relation"}> irreflexivity
              \: for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo #
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# x
              is false;
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"}> symmetry
              \: for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y: S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo #
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y # x
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo #
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x # y
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison"}> comparison
              \: for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y, z: S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo #
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x # z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo #
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x # y
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo #
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y # z
          %p
            (Notice that these are dual to the axioms for an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverses"} inverses
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            in a groupoid.)
          %h3#related_notions Related notions
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            of an apartness relation is an equivalence relation. (On the other hand, the statement that every equivalence relation is the negation of some apartness relation is equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+law"} de Morgan law
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            if this equivalence relation is
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient set
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            are both sets equipped with apartness relations, then a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon S \to T
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+extensional+function"} strongly extensional
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# y
            whenever
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo #
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \# f(y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            reflects apartness. The strongly extensional functions are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            between
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi TV
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV^\op
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is tight.)
          %h2#21category_of_sets_with_apartness_relations (2,1)-category of sets with apartness relations
          %p
            Sets with apartness relations, strongly extensional functions, and equivalences of strongly extensional functions, which serve to identify unequal but equivalent (that is, not apart) elements of a set, form a locally thin
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+bicategory"} enriched
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+groupoids"} thin groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+bicategory"} univalent bicategory
          %h2#apartness_relations_and_equality_of_sets Apartness relations and equality of sets
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            comes with an apartness relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq y
          %p
            However, in constructive mathematics, the usual classical notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            bifurcates into multiple notions which are not equivalent to each other. Here is a Hasse diagram of some of them, applied to the equality and apartness relation, with the strongest statement at the bottom and the weakest at the top (so that each statement entails those above it):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⇗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⇖
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo ←
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⇖
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ⇗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo ←
                          %mo ¬
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∨
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {           &amp;          &amp; \neg(\neg(x = y) \wedge \neg(x \neq y)) \\
                  \&amp; &amp;#x21d7; &amp;          &amp; &amp;#x21d6; \\
                  \\neg(x = y) \rightarrow x \neq y &amp;          &amp;          &amp;          &amp; x = y \leftarrow \neg(x \neq y) \\
                  \&amp; &amp;#x21d6; &amp;          &amp; &amp;#x21d7; \\
                  \&amp;          &amp; (\neg(x = y) \rightarrow x \neq y) \wedge (x = y \leftarrow \neg(x \neq y)) \\
                  \&amp;          &amp; \Uparrow \\
                  \&amp;          &amp; x = y \vee x \neq y }
          %h2#topology Topological aspects
          %h3#the_apartness_topology The apartness topology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a set equipped with an apartness relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topological
            notions may be defined on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
            in topology.)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is an element, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
            (or
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong neighborhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            if, given any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\colon S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            or
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
            by irreflexivity. The neighbourhoods of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            form a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            (hence of any finite number) of neighbourhoods is a neighbourhood.
          %p
            A subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
            if it's a neighbourhood of all of its members. The open subsets form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            (in the sense of Bourbaki): any union of open subsets is open, and the intersection of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            (hence of any finite number) of open subsets is open.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %strong complement
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is the subset
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{y\colon S \;|\; x \ne y\}
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of any subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{A}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{A} \coloneqq \{y \;|\; \forall{x} \in A,\; x \ne y\} .
          %p
            This is not in general open, but you would use it where you would classically use the set-theoretic complement. However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is open to begin with, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{A}
            equals the set-theoretic complement.
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mover
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \tilde{y}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in \tilde{x}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            is tight, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≠
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \ne)
            satisfies the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
            = succeed ")" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                quasi-apartness
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/quasi-apartness"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            topology, but it would not be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
            (or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            might also fail).
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure"} closure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{A}
            of a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the complement of its complement. This closure is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset \bar{A}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\bar{A}} = \bar{A}
            (in fact,
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\tilde{A}} = \tilde{A}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{A} \subset \bar{B}
            whenever
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi S
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{S} = S
            (in fact,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\empty} = \empty
            too), and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∩
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A \cap B} = \bar{A} \cap \bar{B}
            (but
            %em not
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi B
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ∪
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A \cup B} = \bar{A} \cup \bar{B}
          %p
            The
            %strong antigraph
            of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon S \to T
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(x,y) \;|\; x\colon S, y\colon T \;|\; f(x) \ne y\} .
          %p
            Recall that in ordinary topology, a function between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
            is continuous iff its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph
            is closed. Similarly, a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon S \to T
            is strongly extensional iff its antigraph is open. (Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the complement of the antigraph.)
          %p
            One important topological concept that doesn't appear classically is locatedness; in a set with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} tight apartness relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+subspace"} located
            if, given any point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and any neighbourhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \cap A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            (that is, it has a point) or some neighbourhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            (not necessarily
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo #
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\# A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi z
                    %mo #
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall z\in V, a\in A\ [z\# a]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\colon S \;|\; p\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is an arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is true or false.)
          %h3#relation_to_metric_spaces Relation to metric spaces
          %p
            Recall that, as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            taught us, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            is a groupoid (or
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger-category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([0,\infty[^\op,+)
            of nonnegative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "-morphisms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]
            instead of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty[
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([0,\infty[^\op,+)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi TV
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV^\op
            that maps a nonnegative real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to the truth value of the statement that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(f(x),f(y)) \leq d(x,y)
          %p
            The topological properties of metric spaces fit well with those of sets with a tight apartness relation if you always work in this direction. For example, a set which is
            = succeed "-open" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "-open," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            between metric spaces is (still) strongly extensional.
          %h3#relation_to_gauge_spaces_and_uniform_spaces Relation to gauge spaces and uniform spaces
          %p
            In analysis, many spaces are given as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+spaces"} gauge spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) \gt 0
            for some pseudometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            in the family. (This will actually be a
            %em tight
            apartness iff the family of pseudometrics is separating.)
          %p
            Classically, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            may be given by a family of pseudometrics, but this doesn't hold constructively. In particular, a topological group may not be an inequality group (as in the next section). However, we can generalize a bit beyond gauge spaces: any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+regular+uniform+space"} uniformly regular uniform space
            becomes a set with a tight apartness relation by declaring that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne y
            iff there is an entourage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)\notin U
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
          %h3#relation_to_proximity_spaces Relation to proximity spaces
          %p
            The constructive theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+spaces"} proximity spaces
            is based on a generalisation of apartness relations (which here go between
            = succeed ")" do
              %em points
            = succeed "." do
              %em sets
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+space"} apartness spaces
          %p
            Of course, any apartness space has an apartness relation between points:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are apart iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{y\}
            are apart.
          %h3#relation_to_locales Relation to locales
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a set, regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+locale"} discrete locale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            of opens is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(X) = P(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are precisely the subsets of the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+locale"} locally compact
            (every set is the union of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-finite+set"} K-finite
            subsets), the locale product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            agrees with the spatial product, so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            is also discrete and every subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            is open. Thus, the opens in the locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            are precisely the subsets of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            on the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be identified with an
            %em open
            equivalence relation (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Loc
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p Thus, the following theorem gives a different precise sense in which apartness relations are dual to equivalence relations.
          #ClosedLocalicEquivalenceRelation.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              An apartness relation on a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the same as a (strongly)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed
              equivalence relation on the discrete locale
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By definition, a (strongly) closed sublocale of a locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is one of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi C
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in O(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a discrete locale, a closed sublocale of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
              is of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              for some subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mi x
                      %mo #
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \{ (x,y) \mid x\#y \}
            %p
              For the first claim, therefore, it remains to show that the three axioms of an equivalence relation for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              correspond to the apartness axioms for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo #
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi C
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(\mathsf{C}U) = \mathsf{C}(f^*U)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              along the twist map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X \to X\times X
              is the closed sublocale corresponding to the twist of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                      %mi y
                      %mo #
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ (x,y) \mid y\#x \}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}
              is a contravariant order-isomorphism between the posets of open and closed sublocales, symmetry for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              is equivalent to symmetry for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo #
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              back to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X\times X
              along one of the three canonical projections gives the closed sublocale dual to the corresponding pullback of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              itself, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}
              transforms unions to intersections; thus transitivity for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              is equivalent to comparison for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo #
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi C
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{C}U
              along the diagonal is the closed sublocale dual to the similar pullback of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalent to saying that the latter is
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
