          %h2#references References
          %p
            According to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#TvD"} Troelstra and van Dalen
          %blockquote
            %p
              Brouwer (
              %a{:href => "#Brouwer1919"}> 1919
              ) introduced the notion of apartness (örtlich verschieden, Entfernung)…. The axioms of the theory of apartness were formulated by Heyting (
              %a{:href => "#Heyting1925"}> 1925
              ).
          %ul
            %li#Brouwer1919
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.E.J.+Brouwer"}> L.E.J. Brouwer
                ,
                %em Begründung der Mengenlehre unabhängig vom logischen Satz vom ausgeschlossenen Dritten II: Theorie der Punktmengen. 1919
            %li#Heyting1925
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arend+Heyting"}> Arend Heyting
                ,
                %em Intuïtionistische Axiomatiek der Projectieve Meetkunde
                (Dutch), Ph.D. Thesis, 1925
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Errett+Bishop"}> Errett Bishop
                ‘s
                %em Foundations of Constructive Analysis
                (1967) uses apartness for the real numbers and more general metric spaces.
            %li
              %p
                The 1985 edition with Douglas Bridges,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructive Analysis
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
                need not satisfy comparison).
            %li#TvD
              %p
                Anne Troelstra's and Dirk van Dalen's
                %em Constructivism in Mathematics
                (1988) uses apartness for the reals (volume 1), and general apartness relations in algebra (volume 2, chapter 8). They say “preapartness” and “apartness” instead of “apartness” and “tight apartness” respectively.
            %li
              %p
                Apartness plays a minimal role in
                %em A Course in Constructive Algebra
                (also 1988), by Ray Mines, Fred Richman, and Wim Ruitenburg.
            %li
              %p
                A great reference for point-set topology in constructive mathematics is the Ph.D. thesis of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franka+Waaldijk"} Franka Waaldijk
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.fwaaldijk.nl/modern%20intuitionistic%20topology.pdf"} Modern intuitionistic topology
                (1996).
            %li#Shulman2022
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Affine logic for constructive mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/bsl.2022.28"} doi:10.1017/bsl.2022.28
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.07518"} arXiv:1805.07518
